{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1092", "sample_idx": 18, "model_name": "mistralai/ministral-14b-instruct-2512", "content": "**A Whirlwind in Japan: Cherry Blossoms and Sushi**\n\nLast month, I traded city lights for neon-lit streets and ancient temples, exploring Japan’s captivating mix of tradition and modernity. The journey began in **Tokyo**, where salty winds from **Odaiba’s** harbor met towering skyscrapers. Sipping matcha at **Tsukiji Outer Market**, I marveled at the precision of sushi chefs—each cut a work of art. By evening, **Shibuya Crossing** pulsed with life, a symphony of scooters and laughter.\n\nA bullet train whisked me to **Kyoto**, where time seemed to slow. Wandering the **Bamboo Forest** at Arashiyama, sunlight filtered through slender stalks, casting dappled shadows. At **Fushimi Inari**, thousands of red torii gates stretched into the hills—a breathtaking labyrinth. My stay peaked at **Kinkaku-ji**, the Golden Pavilion, shimmering like a mirrored jewel on Kyoto’s horizon.\n\nSpring’s magic unfolded in **Hiroshima**, where **Peace Park** honored history amidst delicate **sakura**. Picking petals from the **Miyajima** island’s floating torii gate, I understood why locals called it *\"momiji\"* (autumn leaves) season’s twin.\n\nFinal stop: **Osaka**, where **Dotonbori’s** giant crab sign and takoyaki stalls beckoned. The trip ended with a ferry ride under **Rainbow Bridge**, fireworks exploding overhead—a perfect farewell.\n\nJapan’s charm lies in its contradictions: serene shrines next to cyber cafés, Michelin-starred tempura beside convenience-store bento. In a week, I fell in love with its rhythm—effortless, poetic, and utterly unforgettable. Already dreaming of my return.", "logprobs": [{"token": "**", "logprob": -0.06550939381122589}, {"token": "A", "logprob": -0.27843376994132996}, {"token": " Wh", "logprob": -0.037113383412361145}, {"token": "irl", "logprob": -0.018043426796793938}, {"token": "wind", "logprob": -4.7801782784517854e-05}